# 7. CREATE TWO DEPTHS OF EXPERIENCE WITHOUT SPLITTING THE PLATFORM

The platform must support both a simple beginner experience and an advanced professional experience.

Do not create two separate products or disconnected copies of functionality.

Instead, introduce a coherent interface that can progressively reveal complexity.

## Guided Experience

Optimized for:

- Grade 6–8 students.
- First-time users.
- Beginners.
- Users with limited digital or reading confidence.

Characteristics:

- Clear next action.
- Simple terminology.
- Visual instructions.
- Step-by-step workflows.
- Beginner-friendly explanations.
- Less unnecessary information shown at once.
- Obvious back and continue controls.

## Full / Advanced Experience

Optimized for:

- Pre-medical students.
- Medical students.
- Researchers.
- Professors.
- Experienced users.

Characteristics:

- Faster navigation.
- Detailed controls.
- Scientific terminology.
- Advanced study dimensions.
- Professional tools.
- Full access to all relevant functionality.

### Crucial rule

Guided Experience must not remove tools.

Advanced Experience must not become a separate application.

A user must be able to move between beginner explanations and advanced detail whenever needed.

Use the existing academic-depth system where appropriate:

- Foundational
- Intermediate
- Advanced

Verify how `depthLevel` currently affects the actual learning content.

Do not merely rename the depth buttons while leaving the content unchanged.

